 {"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:11:41.029564Z","id":"eb75126a93fa8854cf3f7bce204b1decc9c17b2b625e416c92506d54e0ab8bd0","body":{"detail":"The other five agents' projections are byte-stable across runs and pinned raw. If copilot's export ever takes a fixed session id, or toolpath-cursor's `extra`/content_blobs maps become ordered (BTreeMap), drop the canonical form for that agent so the golden is the real bytes `p export -o` writes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"4a694e0ca91a31337ac7971bff42f9e146dbc6c66fe755a12cff8566198c2a4b"},"summary":"Copilot's projection is pinned in canonical form (sorted keys, session id masked) because p export copilot mints a session id per run; Cursor's is pinned with keys sorted because its composer rows carry hash maps written in a different order per run","supersedes":"6c8a2e928b72b113a2fdf76cf4bf050613d257da64221423d52c9d3f7da42c3a","tags":["goldens","determinism","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
 {"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:11:41.052708Z","id":"0d022915b3a3d0a1a35bbc09798295af09631aed1c6888559c49c0c7259b8354","body":{"detail":"test-fixtures/opencode/convo.json is what `opencode export <id>` prints (camelCase, nested info); toolpath_opencode reads rows from opencode-stable.db and has no reader for this file. A `Session::from_export` in the adapter would remove all three copies, and `path p derive opencode` could then take the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":336},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"e1f0854ff123c1ce324417c98893618c5a16b9d4d7c747feadd81bba62cca511"},"summary":"The `opencode export` wrapper to Session translation is duplicated from path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs and toolpath-opencode/tests/real_fixture_roundtrip.rs; the adapter should own it","supersedes":"1ed3cef0bf59d394fde4ae0e8ff308b05f59b10adc79f8b2738b6b78b2aaad88","tags":["goldens","opencode","duplication","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
 {"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:26:48.677927Z","id":"c9e19e1babef8e3a0d85dd27a799216939ec72535e3f7c2c016d50ac9b995bb2","body":{"detail":"Every one of the 42 (source, target) pairs across the seven agents is `compared` today; the Unreadable variant stays for a pair that genuinely cannot be re-read. The round trip also yields the re-derived document for validate@<set>.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":566},"end":{"line":566},"content_hash":"8e1832973f8749c6b919a6aedfc4ea89442e372b5ea88e505414008ed4cea0aa"},"summary":"A round trip that cannot read its own projection is a pinned outcome, not a failed stage; the hermetic tool recorded copilot->claude that way because its placement needed a top-level cwd, in-process the adapter reads it","supersedes":"e89fe8d166931d0c2233e904548fcdc9c8184b18b6610abec48bda442bb8df42","tags":["goldens","round-trip","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
+{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-goldens/src/pipeline.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:49:26.067890Z","id":"98ef9cbd37b7cc86dbbbba1ab5969dda5ff3c2db9956c86b6664bf989d8390aa","body":{"detail":"Not a defect. path resume --harness codex -C <dir> (cmd_resume -> projection::codex::project_codex) and path export codex --project <dir> write the -C/--project directory into session_meta.cwd, every turn_context.cwd and the state_5.sqlite thread row; export -o without --project uses the shell's cwd. That is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables the cwd filter), so the source cwd would hide a resumed session from the picker in the directory the user resumed in, and is usually a path that does not exist on the resuming machine. The goldens wrote / because the hermetic harness runs from / (CALLER_CWD); the pin compared against the source cwd, so a change to write the source cwd would have been judged FIXED while breaking resume. Pin and Finding::CallerCwd removed; contract pinned by path-cli projection::codex::tests::project_codex_writes_the_resume_directory_as_cwd_not_the_source_cwd. pr/22.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"0beee873aef40908b4e7e97e085fcd88e7802bd043a4260b138f92949e0799bd"},"summary":"CALLER_CWD is the directory a projection is resumed in, not a stand-in for a defect: the caller's cwd is the contract for codex, pi, copilot and gemini","supersedes":"2ab7d3eadd1d77ab6800807715c314eefa5042fa785b672dc45ada66cf316667","tags":["goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
